{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant modality (scvi_n200 rna_only: 0.650 vs image_only resnet50: 0.208), and within RNA, scvi_n200 with avgpool aggregation is the best tested encoder (0.650 vs pca_n2000's 0.591). However, scgpt has been completely untested, leaving a major uncertainty about whether a different RNA representation could outperform scvi_n200. Question: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005 (same setup but scvi_n200), isolating the effect of the RNA encoder while holding profile setting and aggregation constant. Why this is the best next experiment: RNA is the primary signal source, so the encoder choice is the highest-leverage design decision. Resolving whether scgpt is competitive with or superior to scvi_n200 before committing further experiments to multimodal scgpt variants (configs 042-051) avoids wasting budget on a potentially inferior encoder. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, it opens a new high-value direction; if not, we can confidently focus remaining experiments on optimizing the scvi_n200 pipeline (e.g., testing imagenet_vit_l as image encoder in the multimodal setting)."
}

